 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Developer diagnostics
+
+The homepage workbench checks a hardware device on a private LAN and a companion
+HTTP service on the reader's computer. All requests originate in the browser,
+only after the reader selects Connect. There is no server-side network proxy.
+
+The endpoint URLs are editable examples, not bundled services. Configure each
+service to expose a health endpoint that accepts GET and returns a 2xx status.
+The response format is unrestricted; the widget verifies reachability rather
+than opening a persistent telemetry stream. Each service must return
+`Access-Control-Allow-Origin` for the deployed site's origin (the origin has no
+path, including no `/devtools-times/`). Credentials are omitted.
+
+Serve the site over HTTPS. Supporting browsers can prompt separately for local
+network and loopback access. Requests declare `targetAddressSpace` as `local` for
+the device and `loopback` for the CLI; unsupported browsers still require their
+normal CORS and mixed-content rules. See the [browser network access guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/security/local-network-access).
+
+Checks time out after 15 seconds, can be canceled, and do not run automatically.
+Activity is held in memory for the current widget session, with a 50-event limit.
